        "original_id": "4152bb0f-858b-583d-b578-8128843bfed1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Herman Boone, Jerry Bruckheimer, Boaz Yakin, Christopher Lloyd, Jeff Daniels, Daryl Hannah, Elizabeth Hurley, Wallace Shawn, Ray Walston, Denzel Washington\n- Films: Remember the Titans, My Favorite Martian\n- TV Series: My Favorite Martian\n- Organizations: T. C. Williams High School football team\n\nFacts:\n- Herman Ike Boone was born on October 28, 1935, and became a former American high school football coach.\n- Ray Walston starred in the 1960s television series My Favorite Martian.\n- In 1971, Herman Boone coached the T. C. Williams High School football team to a 13-0 season, a state championship, and a national championship runner-up finish.\n- My Favorite Martian is a 1999 American science fiction comedy film starring Christopher Lloyd, Jeff Daniels, Daryl Hannah, Elizabeth Hurley, Wallace Shawn, and Ray Walston, and it was based on the 1960s television series of the same name.\n- Remember the Titans and Herman Boone’s 1971 T. C. Williams High School football team story formed a basis for the 2000 film Remember the Titans.\n- Remember the Titans is a 2000 American sports film produced by Jerry Bruckheimer and directed by Boaz Yakin.\n- In Remember the Titans, Denzel Washington portrayed Herman Boone.\n- My Favorite Martian grossed $36.8 million domestically against a budget of $65 million.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
